course: dictionary
lesson: 5653
title: The word list
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A list is a set of words, names or numbers written one after another, often one under another. «Lily starts a list of Aussie words» means she is writing those words down, one after another.
explain: To list things is to write them or say them in order, one after another. You can also be on a list, which means you are included in it, as in «a place on the waiting list». A ship that lists leans to one side, so the same word can mean different things.
explain: In maths, a list is a set of numbers you can count, add, order or find the biggest of. The question tells you what to do with it. In writing, the items in a list are joined by commas.
fact: A list is a set of words, names or numbers written one after another.
fact: To list things means to write them or say them one after another.
fact: «Lily starts a list of Aussie words.» Here list is a noun, a written set of items.
fact: To be on a list means to be included in it, like «on the waiting list».
fact: A ship that lists leans to one side.
exercise: «Lily starts a list of Aussie words.» What is a list? | A type of bread | *A set of words written one after another | A ship that leans to one side | A loud noise
exercise: «The ingredients list tells the truth.» What does the ingredients list show? | A picture of the food on the box | The price of the food | *The things that are in the food, written one after another | The name of the shop
exercise: Dad says, «Put your name on the waiting list.» What does being on a list mean? | Being very tall | Being lost in a crowd | Being spoken to by the teacher | *Being included in it
test: Which is a shopping list? | A game for two players | *A list of things you want to buy | A ship that leans to one side | A map of the shop
test: In maths, what does a list give you to work with? | *Numbers to count, add, order or find the biggest of | Paint the numbers red | Secrets to hide | Songs to sing
exam: In «Please list three animals», what kind of word is list? | A number | An adjective, a describing word | A noun, a naming word | *A verb, a doing word
